## Expected Behavior

TODO: Describe expected behavior

## Actual Behavior

TODO: Describe actual behavior

## Symptom

c2c relay disable (c2c_relay_cmd.ml:743-762) writes enabled:false and stops the systemd unit - but a subscribe-daemon started before disable keeps retrying the parked URL forever (backoff capped at 30s, c2c_relay_subscribe_daemon.ml:365-527; a shutdown command exists but is not invoked or mentioned), and running c2c monitor relay watchers keep their startup-resolved URL. User-visible: continued connections from this host to the supposedly-off relay; the doctor storm check can fire on the daemon.

## Fix direction

relay disable best-effort sends shutdown to the subscribe-daemon socket and prints a line naming both classes of lingering consumers; longer term the daemon and monitor re-check Relay_activation each retry cycle.

## Evidence

CLI review 2026-09-17; verified in source by coordinator.